WEBVTT

00:22.022 --> 00:26.943
IN THE FOOD CHAIN

00:28.236 --> 00:33.491
<i>The UFS Fight Club finals
were held last night at the old market.</i>

00:34.576 --> 00:36.369
<i>The winner was...</i>

00:36.453 --> 00:38.788
That female rabbit again, I'm sure.

00:39.289 --> 00:41.332
<i>That's right. Kyuu.</i>

00:41.416 --> 00:43.293
<i>That's 17 wins in a row.</i>

00:43.835 --> 00:45.962
<i>No one's betting against her anymore.</i>

00:46.046 --> 00:49.132
<i>That rabbit survives in the Black Market.</i>

00:49.215 --> 00:51.259
<i>She's no normal herbivore.</i>

00:52.385 --> 00:57.140
<i>It's been about 10 years since you
liberated the live bait market, right?</i>

00:57.640 --> 01:01.102
<i>Why did Gohin
make that rabbit his pupil anyway?</i>

01:01.603 --> 01:04.606
Beats me. I don't know how pandas think.

01:06.149 --> 01:11.488
<i>On that note, my sources tell me
that Gohin has another pupil.</i>

01:12.238 --> 01:15.325
<i>Our favorite gray wolf.</i>

01:17.118 --> 01:21.706
I see. The kid, huh? Interesting.

01:22.499 --> 01:25.794
<i>There's one more point of interest.</i>

01:25.877 --> 01:28.088
<i>About the sale of elephant ivory.</i>

01:28.171 --> 01:31.132
<i>It's an anonymous tip, but take a look.</i>

01:33.885 --> 01:35.553
Only the tusks are missing.

01:37.889 --> 01:40.016
Zoom in on that pipe.

01:42.727 --> 01:46.523
A 10K gate valve. Yellow.

01:48.608 --> 01:52.111
Those are the same ones used
in the redevelopment of Center Street.

01:52.195 --> 01:53.113
Look into it.

01:53.196 --> 01:54.239
<i>Understood.</i>

01:54.322 --> 01:56.699
We'll stomp them out
as soon as we find them.

02:02.497 --> 02:03.498
Legoshi?

02:05.208 --> 02:06.084
Long time no see!

02:06.167 --> 02:08.962
- How are you?
- Good. It's been a while.

02:09.462 --> 02:11.673
Were you meeting
about the Festival of the Meteor?

02:11.756 --> 02:14.384
Well, it was supposed to be.

02:15.844 --> 02:19.013
The drama club has been
split into carnivores and herbivores,

02:19.639 --> 02:21.766
and we still haven't
written up a proposal.

02:22.559 --> 02:26.688
So now it might be held at
another school this year.

02:28.022 --> 02:31.151
I see... Even the clubs
have been segregated?

02:31.234 --> 02:33.528
Haven't you heard anything?

02:33.611 --> 02:34.779
What do we do?

02:35.280 --> 02:37.866
We'll have to think of something.

02:37.949 --> 02:40.827
Sorry. I've got to go meet my boyfriend.

02:43.454 --> 02:44.455
Bye!

02:44.539 --> 02:45.540
Later.

02:47.167 --> 02:49.043
"Help me out"? What does that mean?

02:53.172 --> 02:54.591
This is what you meant?

02:54.674 --> 02:58.553
Manual labor is about all you're good for.

02:58.636 --> 03:00.763
You could have asked Aoba or Tao.

03:00.847 --> 03:04.142
Shut up. They were busy, okay?

03:04.934 --> 03:06.895
What about the herbivores?

03:07.604 --> 03:09.689
I'm sure they would have helped.

03:09.772 --> 03:11.316
Maybe.

03:12.066 --> 03:13.484
But you know,

03:14.235 --> 03:18.406
I just feel more comfortable
around other carnivores.

03:19.449 --> 03:23.328
They're trying to blame the carnivores
for the school segregating.

03:23.411 --> 03:28.207
It's not like we chose to be carnivores,
so where do they get off?

03:29.709 --> 03:31.044
But sure,

03:31.127 --> 03:34.172
I love all my herbivore friends too.

03:36.799 --> 03:39.844
Why did you drop out, anyway?

03:40.845 --> 03:42.347
If you were still around,

03:43.056 --> 03:45.850
I could've watched you screw things up
worse than me

03:45.934 --> 03:48.478
and used that as a reference
for what not to do.

03:49.103 --> 03:53.274
<i>He still isn't the nicest guy,
but he's definitely changed.</i>

04:00.907 --> 04:02.200
Is there any point to this?

04:02.909 --> 04:06.496
I mean, will we even get to
be in this year's Festival of the Meteor?

04:06.579 --> 04:07.664
Good question.

04:10.291 --> 04:11.584
It's Legoshi.

04:13.002 --> 04:14.754
What are you doing here?

04:14.837 --> 04:18.299
He may have dropped out of school,
but he hasn't quit the club yet.

04:18.967 --> 04:20.093
What are you talking about?

04:20.176 --> 04:22.011
Hey, Legoshi!

04:22.095 --> 04:24.180
Legoshi! It's been a while!

04:24.931 --> 04:25.765
What's this for?

04:25.848 --> 04:28.434
It's a partition, duh.

04:28.518 --> 04:31.646
- For the club room?
- Good thinking, man!

04:31.729 --> 04:34.023
We'll use it to divide the room into two.

04:34.649 --> 04:36.943
Do you think the teachers will allow it?

04:37.527 --> 04:41.948
We'll have to force them to,
if we want to make the festival happen.

04:42.031 --> 04:45.118
Did something happen at the meeting?

04:45.201 --> 04:47.996
Let's just take this thing inside for now.

04:48.079 --> 04:50.456
Sorry, I have to get to work.

04:51.374 --> 04:53.668
I'll be rooting for you.

04:55.545 --> 04:57.046
Don't get all mushy on me now!

04:57.630 --> 04:58.631
Good luck, guys.

04:59.132 --> 05:00.341
Come visit us again!

05:01.384 --> 05:03.094
He has a job?

05:03.177 --> 05:04.887
I wonder what he does?

05:05.430 --> 05:07.849
Well, we can rule out customer service.

05:15.606 --> 05:17.859
<i>The bloody stench of the Black Market.</i>

05:19.193 --> 05:20.153
<i>It's dreadful.</i>

05:22.196 --> 05:23.031
<i>And yet...</i>

05:23.906 --> 05:25.366
<i>somehow, it calms me.</i>

05:27.660 --> 05:29.120
<i>Pathetic.</i>

05:29.203 --> 05:31.414
<i>If he saw me wavering like this,</i>

05:32.248 --> 05:34.042
<i>what would Ibuki say?</i>

05:35.835 --> 05:36.836
Louis!

05:38.338 --> 05:39.339
Legoshi.

05:41.299 --> 05:43.009
You're all dressed up.

05:43.092 --> 05:44.927
I'm delivering udon.

05:47.013 --> 05:48.681
Oh, this?

05:51.017 --> 05:52.018
Cool, right?

05:52.101 --> 05:53.728
Best part is, it can't be eaten.

05:55.021 --> 05:56.147
I'm joking.

05:56.647 --> 05:58.357
So don't give me that gloomy look.

05:58.983 --> 06:00.109
Sorry.

06:01.069 --> 06:04.489
You're in college now, right?

06:05.031 --> 06:07.241
I've got a lot of obligations, unlike you.

06:08.910 --> 06:11.120
You have more scars on your face.

06:11.704 --> 06:13.581
You're one intimidating delivery guy.

06:14.373 --> 06:15.583
Oh, well...

06:15.666 --> 06:18.169
You never change, do you?

06:20.213 --> 06:21.589
<i>Seeing him like this...</i>

06:22.799 --> 06:27.637
<i>It makes me wonder all over again,
how can herbivores be so elegant?</i>

06:29.097 --> 06:33.017
<i>To coexist with herbivores,
to protect them,</i>

06:33.893 --> 06:38.940
<i>I feel like I would sacrifice anything.</i>

06:42.151 --> 06:43.069
Louis.

06:43.986 --> 06:47.115
I've realized
something terrible about myself.

06:49.408 --> 06:50.910
Up until recently,

06:51.619 --> 06:54.080
I thought I was driven
by my own sense of justice,

06:54.163 --> 06:58.126
that I was fulfilling my responsibility
as a strong carnivore by fighting.

06:59.460 --> 07:01.129
But it wasn't that at all.

07:01.629 --> 07:02.630
The truth is,

07:03.840 --> 07:07.218
all I was driven by
were my kinks and fetishes.

07:07.802 --> 07:09.679
I'm just a violent, perverted wolf.

07:10.513 --> 07:12.682
I don't know a thing about justice.

07:13.683 --> 07:14.767
Come on.

07:14.851 --> 07:17.437
You're just realizing this now?
You dumb dog.

07:18.813 --> 07:22.233
Everyone knows you're a perverted wolf.

07:22.316 --> 07:24.360
The only reason you even like Haru

07:24.444 --> 07:28.573
is because she's the first
female herbivore that ever came onto you.

07:29.657 --> 07:31.451
All guys are like that.

07:31.993 --> 07:35.163
Kinks included, that's just who you are.

07:36.539 --> 07:38.583
Perverted freak or not,

07:39.083 --> 07:42.795
if there's something you want to protect,
I think that counts as justice.

07:43.671 --> 07:44.672
Louis...

07:45.590 --> 07:48.176
Say something, pervert!

07:48.801 --> 07:49.802
Man up!

07:53.723 --> 07:54.724
Right here.

07:54.807 --> 07:56.100
- Are you sure?
- Really?

07:56.184 --> 07:57.894
You sure this is the right way?

07:57.977 --> 07:59.979
The moon is in
the same position as before.

08:00.730 --> 08:02.982
Look. The whiskers
are pointing in this direction.

08:03.858 --> 08:06.777
Is there anyone here that
hasn't pulled their whiskers out?

08:09.238 --> 08:13.826
When I see the moon, I remember
the time Louis and I duked it out.

08:13.910 --> 08:15.369
I wonder how he's doing?

08:15.953 --> 08:18.998
Even as a deer he's more lion than us.

08:19.499 --> 08:20.791
Yeah.

08:20.875 --> 08:24.212
Our new boss may have
gotten the Shishi-Gumi back on our feet,

08:25.004 --> 08:26.881
but something doesn't feel right.

08:27.507 --> 08:28.591
- What's wrong?
- Shit!

08:29.175 --> 08:30.343
I stepped in shit.

08:30.426 --> 08:31.385
Begone, evil spirits!

08:32.345 --> 08:33.387
Just my luck.

08:33.471 --> 08:34.388
Left.

08:37.934 --> 08:39.894
We're back in business thanks to Kines.

08:39.977 --> 08:44.232
The junkies hooked on it are flocking to
the Black Market to get their meat fix,

08:44.315 --> 08:46.817
and we're finally starting
to get some recognition.

08:46.901 --> 08:48.194
All thanks to the boss.

08:49.487 --> 08:50.655
Got a problem?

08:50.738 --> 08:56.202
Well, we as lions
have dignity and distinction.

08:56.285 --> 08:59.205
The boss doesn't quite have that.

08:59.288 --> 09:03.417
He treats the meat of his victims
as nothing but a bite to eat.

09:03.501 --> 09:05.836
And he's such a messy eater.

09:05.920 --> 09:08.756
He doesn't have any table manners.

09:08.839 --> 09:10.132
And you do?

09:10.216 --> 09:12.677
What would Ibuki say if he were alive?

09:13.261 --> 09:16.556
This next plan oughta work.

09:16.639 --> 09:19.600
There was talk of a masquerade party.
What's that about?

09:19.684 --> 09:25.064
That's where you put on a mask
and get up to all sorts of trouble!

09:25.940 --> 09:27.984
Have a little Kines, perhaps?

09:28.067 --> 09:30.736
They're going to reveal
a new drug, apparently.

09:30.820 --> 09:35.283
Let's get out of here
and meet up with this Deshico guy.

09:35.366 --> 09:37.868
Maybe they'll let us have a leg or two.

09:40.705 --> 09:41.706
There's the exit.

09:42.206 --> 09:45.334
You can always trust
your feline instincts.

09:56.929 --> 09:59.890
It only took you three hours
to get through the maze?

09:59.974 --> 10:01.726
That's our Shishi-Gumi.

10:01.809 --> 10:04.604
Don't mock the power of our whiskers.

10:05.271 --> 10:08.649
The feline family
is often associated with mysticism,

10:08.733 --> 10:13.029
but lions, tigers, wildcats, jaguars...

10:13.112 --> 10:15.406
They're all a bunch of oafs.

10:15.489 --> 10:17.491
Nothing mystic about them.

10:18.367 --> 10:19.452
That's right.

10:19.535 --> 10:22.371
Though I am known to some
as the ghost cat...

10:23.080 --> 10:27.293
- You can call me Deshico the civet.
- You're just a kid!

10:27.376 --> 10:29.253
Enjoy your coffee before it gets cold.

10:36.385 --> 10:39.722
I'll teach you just how mystic
we civets are.

10:40.681 --> 10:43.643
We carefully select and eat coffee beans

10:43.726 --> 10:47.229
which make for an exquisite cup of joe
called <i>kopi luwak.</i>

10:47.730 --> 10:49.357
The very coffee you are drinking

10:49.440 --> 10:52.943
is made from beans
eaten and excreted by yours truly.

10:53.027 --> 10:54.236
What?

10:54.820 --> 10:55.905
You mean...

10:57.198 --> 10:58.866
That's right. Poop.

11:00.201 --> 11:01.827
We drank your shit? You bastard!

11:03.329 --> 11:05.873
That's not all we can do.

11:06.374 --> 11:11.170
The liquid secreted from our anuses
is a treasured ingredient for perfume.

11:12.380 --> 11:16.258
Why do all my talents
have to be down here?

11:17.093 --> 11:18.761
It used to get me down,

11:19.261 --> 11:23.724
but then I realized that everything
that passes through me turns to gold.

11:24.975 --> 11:28.104
Now, I'm proud to be me.

11:33.484 --> 11:34.693
It looks like it's working.

11:35.653 --> 11:36.737
What'd you do?

11:37.905 --> 11:43.786
This coffee is 98% water.
The other two percent is the beans.

11:44.412 --> 11:47.081
That dose alone
has a narcotic meat effect similar to,

11:47.164 --> 11:49.917
if not even greater than, that of Kines.

11:50.000 --> 11:52.378
So this is what Boss was after?

11:53.671 --> 11:58.592
The potent properties of elephant ivory,
the bones and meat of animals,

11:59.593 --> 12:02.012
blood gathered by these cuties,

12:02.513 --> 12:04.932
and of course, my <i>kopi luwak.</i>

12:05.015 --> 12:09.395
Blended together and purified,
you get this beautiful black jewel.

12:09.478 --> 12:10.438
Melda.

12:10.521 --> 12:11.939
Melda?

12:12.022 --> 12:14.150
Known as "deer shit" on the streets.

12:14.233 --> 12:17.111
Nothing compares to this.

12:18.112 --> 12:23.367
Your boss, Melon,
is asking for tons of this stuff.

12:23.868 --> 12:27.455
So this is the new drug
for the masquerade party.

12:35.421 --> 12:37.006
It smells so good.

12:37.631 --> 12:40.384
Thanks. That's my poop.

12:41.177 --> 12:42.386
- No!
- Begone, evil spirits!

12:42.470 --> 12:45.389
The maze out there
is made of coffee trees.

12:45.473 --> 12:47.433
You'll find it's filled with droppings.

12:47.516 --> 12:50.436
I'd like you to collect it all
and bring it to me tonight.

12:50.519 --> 12:51.812
Why would we do that?

12:51.896 --> 12:54.398
The king of the beasts
doesn't pick up shit.

12:54.482 --> 12:56.317
I told Melon,

12:56.400 --> 12:59.945
we can start production
only if we find the help.

13:00.029 --> 13:01.238
Didn't he tell you that?

13:02.323 --> 13:03.365
That bastard.

13:03.449 --> 13:04.492
We're leaving.

13:07.620 --> 13:11.248
I could always ask
the Madara-Gumi or Inari-Gumi for help.

13:16.253 --> 13:17.213
Damn it.

13:17.296 --> 13:18.964
Everyone! Whiskers out!

13:25.888 --> 13:28.098
"Legoshi the gray wolf,

13:28.182 --> 13:32.978
I am grateful for your cooperation
in the apprehension of a criminal.

13:33.062 --> 13:38.442
I would like to ask a brave man like you
about the state of the city.

13:38.526 --> 13:41.904
Join me for dinner. Yahya."

13:47.284 --> 13:48.994
Excuse me... Here.

13:50.204 --> 13:51.205
What is this?

13:53.874 --> 13:54.708
YAHYA

13:56.085 --> 13:57.711
Please, come in!

14:01.882 --> 14:05.261
<i>I wonder what kind of animal Mr. Yahya is?</i>

14:06.387 --> 14:10.307
<i>What species?
Is he a carnivore? Or an herbivore?</i>

14:32.705 --> 14:34.582
Wow!

14:35.207 --> 14:37.585
There's the Balaena River.

14:37.668 --> 14:39.670
Is that the Kustos Bridge?

14:39.753 --> 14:41.672
And there's my apartment!

14:42.256 --> 14:43.716
It's so small.

14:46.427 --> 14:48.512
Quite the view, isn't it?

14:50.556 --> 14:52.600
Welcome, Legoshi.

14:54.476 --> 14:57.688
Nice to meet you. Are you Mr. Yahya?

14:58.272 --> 15:00.274
Sorry for calling you out here.

15:00.774 --> 15:02.985
Did the staff downstairs treat you okay?

15:03.652 --> 15:04.653
Yes.

15:07.698 --> 15:12.328
I wanted to serve you
these special carrots tonight.

15:13.120 --> 15:16.457
Though perhaps
it does not befit a wolf's tastes?

15:16.540 --> 15:19.168
No, it's great. Thank you.

15:20.628 --> 15:21.629
So...

15:23.714 --> 15:27.176
Mr. Yahya, are you a Beastar?

15:27.801 --> 15:29.261
What makes you think that?

15:29.345 --> 15:32.806
Sorry, I'm just speculating.

15:34.016 --> 15:37.102
You have your own room
on the top floor of the police station.

15:37.645 --> 15:39.480
It's like you're in charge of the police.

15:39.563 --> 15:40.731
But most of all,

15:40.814 --> 15:43.233
these carrots are amazing!

15:43.943 --> 15:46.278
They're sweet and a little earthy,

15:46.362 --> 15:48.280
but chewy in texture.

15:48.364 --> 15:51.325
It's like the more you chew them...
How do I put it?

15:51.408 --> 15:53.702
I've never had carrots like these before!

15:53.786 --> 15:55.955
If you're always eating
amazing food like this,

15:56.038 --> 15:59.166
I figure you must be someone important...

15:59.249 --> 16:01.710
That's all. Sorry.

16:04.213 --> 16:06.382
I'm glad you're enjoying them.

16:06.924 --> 16:10.469
Yes, these carrots are indeed special.

16:12.096 --> 16:14.348
They're grown
at just the right temperature

16:14.431 --> 16:17.601
and cared for with
special water and nutrients.

16:18.227 --> 16:22.022
Perfection is born
from the perfect environment.

16:23.399 --> 16:26.568
Don't you think
society should be the same?

16:27.695 --> 16:31.031
<i>I can't be totally certain,</i>

16:31.115 --> 16:34.284
<i>but I'm pretty sure
Mr. Yahya is a Beastar.</i>

16:35.244 --> 16:37.371
<i>His body is like a tall tower.</i>

16:37.871 --> 16:40.541
<i>Just how much power does he have?</i>

16:42.042 --> 16:44.586
Let me show you something before dessert.

16:50.050 --> 16:51.218
For me,

16:51.760 --> 16:54.471
in order for a perfect society
to be realized,

16:54.555 --> 16:57.266
I'm willing to bear
any hardship or sacrifice.

16:59.727 --> 17:00.728
Legoshi.

17:01.770 --> 17:05.357
What do you think a Beastar is?

17:07.192 --> 17:08.360
Well...

17:09.528 --> 17:14.742
Carnivore or herbivore,
everyone has their own struggles.

17:15.284 --> 17:21.165
But I think what keeps them going is hope.
And that's what a Beastar is.

17:21.248 --> 17:26.712
I guess it's kind of an ideal
that everyone has within them.

17:26.795 --> 17:28.213
Or something like that.

17:29.673 --> 17:31.050
I see.

17:31.884 --> 17:35.846
But Beastars are something
much more pragmatic.

17:37.931 --> 17:39.308
They are not hope.

17:40.142 --> 17:43.187
Beastars are order and discipline.

17:44.063 --> 17:45.481
Order and discipline?

17:46.899 --> 17:51.987
I actually kind of like
society's imperfections.

17:52.488 --> 17:55.074
But the reason
that this imperfect society can exist

17:55.157 --> 17:56.867
is all because of you, Mr. Yahya!

17:56.950 --> 17:58.035
You're amazing.

17:58.786 --> 18:04.124
<i>A polite, well-mannered,
carefree young wolf.</i>

18:04.958 --> 18:06.543
<i>What a brat.</i>

18:08.170 --> 18:11.882
Don't you find it odd, Legoshi?

18:12.466 --> 18:17.387
Don't you wonder how one horse
can fight society's evils like I have?

18:18.013 --> 18:19.473
Do you work out?

18:20.015 --> 18:22.893
I do, but you still need
an energy source to work out, no?

18:24.186 --> 18:29.233
When you become a Beastar,
you are granted one wish.

18:31.819 --> 18:33.529
Even if that wish

18:33.612 --> 18:39.201
is turning carnivores
that you've punished into fertilizer.

18:39.660 --> 18:42.454
Like you, Legoshi,
with your record of devouring,

18:46.458 --> 18:49.920
these carrots greedily devoured
the nutrients they were granted.

18:50.003 --> 18:52.047
You must have found them delicious!

18:54.091 --> 18:55.134
Whoa, now.

18:56.301 --> 18:57.427
You're not going anywhere.

19:08.522 --> 19:12.609
Surely you aren't judging me, are you?

19:12.693 --> 19:15.320
I know all about you.

19:15.404 --> 19:19.491
To win a fight
against your devourer classmate,

19:19.575 --> 19:23.871
you ate your deer friend's leg, correct?

19:23.954 --> 19:25.622
That's some determination.

19:26.123 --> 19:30.419
Do you consider your actions good or evil?

19:33.172 --> 19:35.257
<i>Well, Gosha?</i>

19:38.802 --> 19:44.141
A mammal and a reptile?
Society will never accept mixed bloods!

19:44.808 --> 19:45.893
You may be right.

19:46.476 --> 19:53.317
But all families have their problems.
I want to experience that.

19:53.400 --> 19:58.947
The happiness that lies beyond the pain
is what I want.

19:59.990 --> 20:03.202
It's the tiny dream of a venomous lizard.

20:03.285 --> 20:04.828
Can't you accept that?

20:05.454 --> 20:07.539
<i>I can't, Gosha.</i>

20:08.874 --> 20:11.501
<i>Look what your hunger for love
has brought you.</i>

20:11.585 --> 20:14.546
<i>Now, your beloved grandson is here,</i>

20:15.088 --> 20:18.592
<i>at the mercy of my judgment.</i>

20:23.347 --> 20:25.557
I'll tell you this.

20:29.436 --> 20:35.025
To escape danger in the adult world,
you've got to show sincerity.

20:35.734 --> 20:37.027
Sincerity?

20:38.820 --> 20:41.073
Beg for my forgiveness.

20:41.615 --> 20:48.247
No matter the reason, a Beastar cannot
forgive the act of eating living meat.

20:49.081 --> 20:53.585
But if you were to
prostrate yourself before me,

20:53.669 --> 20:58.090
and apologize for being born a carnivore,

20:58.173 --> 21:03.595
you may prevent some of your peers
from becoming fertilizer for my garden.

21:04.388 --> 21:06.765
So, get on your hands and knees.

21:09.142 --> 21:12.980
<i>I ate Louis's leg so I could beat Riz.</i>

21:14.439 --> 21:16.942
<i>Apologize for being born a carnivore?</i>

21:17.943 --> 21:20.153
<i>It's on, Gosha.</i>

21:20.779 --> 21:25.200
<i>Which one of us was right back then?</i>

21:30.205 --> 21:34.334
For being born a carnivore
and eating my friend's leg,

21:35.711 --> 21:36.837
I sincerely apologize.

21:38.422 --> 21:39.923
Even if he did consent,

21:41.258 --> 21:42.718
I know what I did is unforgivable.

21:45.387 --> 21:47.556
It pains me every day.

21:50.183 --> 21:51.768
I'll carry this burden forever.

21:58.025 --> 21:59.484
And so...

22:01.528 --> 22:03.280
from this day forward...

22:05.240 --> 22:06.700
I have no use for my fangs.

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
